statement:
You have two unmarked jugs that hold `x` and `y` liters, both empty at the start, and as much water as you want. You may repeat these moves in any order and as many times as you like:

- fill one jug to the brim;
- pour all the water out of one jug;
- pour from one jug into the other, stopping as soon as the receiving jug is full or the giving jug is empty.

Return `true` if the two jugs can ever hold exactly `target` liters between them, and `false` otherwise.

validator:
function validate([x, y, target]) {
  for (const [name, value] of [['x', x], ['y', y], ['target', target]]) {
    if (!Number.isInteger(value) || value < 1 || value > 1000) return `${name} must be a whole number from 1 to 1000.`;
  }
  return null;
}

